{% doc %}
  Pins the shared Manrope heading font on every brand / vehicle / model page
  heading so all of them match the typography established on the policy pages.

  Why this snippet exists: assets/critical.css forces the display serif
  (Cormorant Garamond) onto ALL h1-h6 through

    body :is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6) {
      font-family: var(--font-heading--family) !important;
    }

  That !important rule out-ranks any plain font-family declaration in the
  component styles, so vehicle / brand / model headings silently rendered in
  a serif. Every selector below pairs "body" with a component class and sets
  !important, which gives it higher specificity than the global heading rule
  and makes it independent of stylesheet load order -- Manrope can therefore
  never be overridden by critical.css or any other global heading rule.

  Renders no visible markup; it only contributes one shared stylesheet
  ({% stylesheet %} content is de-duplicated when the snippet is rendered
  more than once on a page). Only the font FAMILY is pinned here -- sizes,
  weights, colors, spacing and layout stay owned by each component.

  Include it from any snippet or section that renders brand, vehicle or
  model headings:

    {% render 'vehicle-heading-font' %}

  Currently rendered by: all-brands-content, shop-by-car-content,
  shop-by-car-models, car-results-content and the autodrape-car-models
  section (All Brands, Shop by Car, every brand model page, every car
  results page and the homepage brand strip).
{% enddoc %}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Shared Manrope heading typography for all brand & vehicle pages.
     Same stack as assets/policy-page.css so the heading systems match. */
  body .autodrape-all-brands__header h1,
  body .shop-by-car-page__header h1,
  body .shop-by-car-models__hero-title,
  body .shop-by-car-models .shop-by-car-models__card-title,
  body .car-results__model,
  body .car-results__shade-heading,
  body .ad-brands__heading h2 {
    font-family: 'Manrope', 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif !important;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
